    "caption": "This looks like the English word claim, but in Japan it usually means a complaint.\n\nクレーム (くれーむ) = a complaint.\nお客様からクレームが来ました。 = We got a complaint from a customer.\nクレームをつける = to make a complaint.\n苦情 (くじょう) = a more formal word for complaint.\n\nFollow for daily Japanese you can actually use.",
